<title>UK: BAA air cargo tonnage up 5.6 pct in Oct.</title>
<headline>BAA air cargo tonnage up 5.6 pct in Oct.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-11-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>British airports operator BAA Plc said on Monday that total air cargo tonnage handled at its seven UK airports rose by 5.6 percent in October compared with a year ago.</p>
<p>BAA said that cargo tonnage at Heathrow was up just 0.5 percent, while Gatwick and Stanstead improved by 20.6 and 29.4 percent respectively. Cargo for the total London area rose 5.7 percent in October compared with a year ago.</p>
<p>Elsewhere, cargo at Edinburgh rose 36.3 percent while Glasgow declined 26.1 percent.</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 4019</p>
